     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear Zhou,<div><br></div><div>Sorry for inconvenience.</div><div>From this error message, I suspect that installation seems not completely or input format has problem. Could you share two files with me?</div><div> 1. &#39;msstats.log&#39; file under the folder which has .sky file</div><div> 2. msstats input file : you can generate File&gt; Export &gt; Report &gt; choose &#39;MSstats input&#39;. Then you can set up the location and file name for this MSstats input file. Then &#39;MSstats input.csv&#39; file can be generated.</div><div><br></div><div>If you can share with these files (you can post here or send me directly), it will be helpful for finding the issue.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div><br></div><div>--Meena </div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "Gdq1LlOfmtAJ",
   "from": "Zhou Baojin",
   "author": "271ac25222d2625e",
   "date": "2015-01-29T01:57:42Z",
   "subject": "Re: error in dataProcess and error in quantData$GROUP_ORIGINAL",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks you Meena，<div>I think there is a problem on the input file title which is determined by Skyline as described in appendix. For example, there is space in the &quot;Protein Name&quot; (ProteinName). The MSstats require &quot;Intensity&quot; and skyline output &quot;Area&quot;. </div><div><br></div><div>I use R script with &quot;MSstats.daily&quot; package instead of Skyline to run the MSstats. It seems more powerful.</div><div><br></div><div>Best Regards</div><div>Baojin</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
